  "question": {
    "text": "Let the complex numbers <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math> are the vertices <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>B</mi></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi></math> respectively of an isosceles right-angled triangle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi></math>&nbsp;with right angle at <math><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo></math> then the value of&nbsp;<math><mfrac><mrow><msup><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mrow><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mrow><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfenced><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mrow><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfrac></math> is equal to",
